// unified value destructor: frees whatever heap a value tag owns (string 1,
// object 3, vector/array 4, map 5, bind 7; int/float own nothing). Forward slot
// so the early ciVarDrop / ciVecClear can dispatch through it and recurse into
// nested containers. THE fix for the cross-run + scope-exit container leak.
#stack[int, 64] ciValFree;
